    {
      "title": "Dilution",
      "excerpt": "DILUTION Our\nhistorical net tangible book value as of June 30, 2026 was approximately US$29.419 million, or US$1.80 per ordinary share. Net tangible\nbook value is total assets less total liabilities, intangible assets and goodwill. Net tangible book value per ordinary share is net\ntangible book value divided by the aggregate number of Class A and Class B ordinary shares outstanding, which have the same economic\nrights except as described under \u201cDescription of Securities We Are Offering.\u201d Our calculation deducts US$30.665 million of\nintangible assets, net, and US$0.791 million of goodwill from reported shareholders\u2019 equity of US$60.875 million and uses 16,216,825\nClass A and 110,000 Class B ordinary shares outstanding at June 30, 2026, or 16,326,825 ordinary shares in total. These historical figures\nalready reflect the March 2025 reverse split. Our\npro forma net tangible book value as of ",
